Convert vector storage through Address_To_Access_Conversions (riscv64)

Langkit_Support and the bootstrap Liblktlang are built in dev mode with
-gnatwe, so any warning is fatal.  Vectors.To_Pointer turned the System.Address
returned by Alloc/Realloc into a pointer to Internal_Elements_Array with an
Unchecked_Conversion.  On targets that need strict alignment GNAT checks the
alignment of the source (System.Address: 8) against that of the designated
array type, and for arrays of records such as AdaSAT's Watcher that is 16 on
riscv64:

    warning: source alignment (8) < alignment of "Internal_Elements_Array" (16)
    warning: in instantiation at liblktlang_adasat-dpll.adb:50
    warning: in instantiation at liblktlang_adasat-vectors.adb:57

which stops liblktlang-implementation.adb from compiling.  (pragma Warnings
Off, on the function or around it, does not silence this check.)

Go through System.Address_To_Access_Conversions instead: the conversion of the
address then happens in the Ada runtime, and the remaining conversion is
between two access types to the same array type, which have the same
alignment.  Nothing changes at run time: the same address, a thin pointer
either way, memory that Alloc returns suitably aligned.

The same declaration is in three places: Langkit_Support.Vectors, its
bootstrap copy Liblktlang_Support.Vectors, and the bootstrap copy of AdaSAT's
Vectors (Liblktlang_AdaSAT.Vectors).

--- a/langkit/support/langkit_support-vectors.ads
+++ b/langkit/support/langkit_support-vectors.ads
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 with Ada.Unchecked_Deallocation;
 
 with System;
+with System.Address_To_Access_Conversions;
 
 --  .. note:: This unit is internal: only Langkit and Langkit-generated
 --  libraries are supposed to use it.
@@ -199,8 +200,20 @@
    subtype Internal_Elements_Array is Elements_Array (Index_Type);
    type Elements_Array_Access is access all Internal_Elements_Array;
 
-   function To_Pointer is
-     new Ada.Unchecked_Conversion (System.Address, Elements_Array_Access);
+   --  Convert through System.Address_To_Access_Conversions: converting a bare
+   --  System.Address (alignment 8) directly to a pointer to an array whose
+   --  alignment is 16 draws the warning "source alignment (8) < alignment of
+   --  Internal_Elements_Array (16)" on targets that need strict alignment
+   --  (riscv64), and warnings are errors here.  The memory comes from Alloc
+   --  and is suitably aligned.
+   package Address_Conversions is
+     new System.Address_To_Access_Conversions (Internal_Elements_Array);
+
+   function To_Access is new Ada.Unchecked_Conversion
+     (Address_Conversions.Object_Pointer, Elements_Array_Access);
+
+   function To_Pointer (Addr : System.Address) return Elements_Array_Access
+   is (To_Access (Address_Conversions.To_Pointer (Addr)));
 
    procedure Free is new Ada.Unchecked_Deallocation
      (Internal_Elements_Array, Elements_Array_Access);
